[h1]Spire Mentor: an AI coach for Slay the Spire 2[/h1]

Spire Mentor rates your options while you play: a score on every card in hand, a ranked list of the moves the AI considered, a win-chance bar, and the map route it likes. Combat advice comes from a Monte Carlo tree search over a full simulation of the fight; map, card-reward, shop, event and rest-site advice comes from a trained run policy. It can also take a single decision for you, or play on by itself until you stop it.

[b]Instinct[/b] (new): for Ironclad on game v0.111.0 and v0.113.0 the advice comes by default from one trained network that makes every decision of the run, fights included, without a search. Switch between Search and Instinct in the badge or with [b]Shift+F8[/b].

It has two styles, picked in the badge's [b]Mode[/b] switch:
[list]
[*][b]Hints[/b] (the default): its opinion while you decide: card scores, ranked moves, the win-chance bar and map markers. Each can be switched off in the settings.
[*][b]Coach[/b]: nothing shows before you act, so you play your own game. Press [b]F5[/b] to peek at its pick for the next decision. After a turn that cost HP or win chance, or a choice it clearly disagrees with, a small note shows what it would have done and why.
[/list]

[b]The coach switches on when the game starts and never plays for you unless you ask.[/b] Press [b]F8[/b] to switch it off (the game is then vanilla: no HUD, no AI, no changed behaviour), [b]F1[/b] for every key. To keep it off at launch, untick [i]Turn the coach on when the game starts[/i] in the mod settings.

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Windows only.[/b] The AI runs as a bundled Windows program (SimAdvisor.exe). On Mac or Linux the mod loads but the coach cannot start.
[*][b]Game builds v0.107.1, v0.111.0 and v0.113.0 (public beta).[/b] On v0.113.0 the advice is approximate and The Fool is not supported yet. A game update can break the mod until a new version is out.
[*][b]BaseLib[/b] (by Alchyr), which Steam installs alongside this mod as a required item.
[/list]

[h2]Keys[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]F1[/b] help: mode, keys, file locations
[*][b]F8[/b] AI coach on / off (from Autopilot: take the controls back)
[*][b]Shift+F8[/b] advisor brain: Search / Instinct
[*][b]F5[/b] Coach style: peek at the AI's pick for just the next decision
[*][b]F6[/b] let the AI take just this one decision
[*][b]Shift+F6[/b] co-op: an AI partner that is waiting for you plays its turn now
[*][b]F7[/b] let the AI keep playing until you press F7 again. It pauses and hands a decision back to you when it has no real policy for it (F7 resumes).
[*][b]Shift+F7[/b] autobattle: the AI plays the fights, you make every run-level decision (card rewards, map, shops, rest sites, events), with a note at each one on what changed since the last. Press again to stop.
[*][b]F4[/b] show / hide the HUD
[*][b]Ctrl+L[/b] action log: what was played, and what was advised at the time
[*][b]Ctrl+H[/b] hide every panel for a quick look (again, or click the badge, to bring them back)
[*][b]F9 / F10[/b] game speed down / up (1x to 8x)
[*][b]Ctrl+Z[/b] undo to the start of this combat turn
[*][b]Ctrl+Shift+Z[/b] rewind to the start of this room
[*][b]Ctrl+Shift+C[/b] copy this position, to paste into the workbench
[*][b]Ctrl+Shift+B[/b] report a bug (see below)
[/list]
The [b]Spire Mentor[/b] badge under the right end of the top bar does the same with the mouse: click it for the mode, the brain, the AI controls, game speed and the [b]Rewind[/b], [b]Panels[/b] and [b]Workbench[/b] menus. Drag its grip to move it.

The coach's panels open in [b]their own window[/b] around the game, so they never cover the board. [b]⛶ Fullscreen[/b] there fills the screen; [b]⛶ Exit fullscreen[/b] beside the badge goes back. Close that window to put them back in the game.

Settings: [b]Panels → Settings[/b] on the toolbar (works mid-run), or Main menu → Options → Mod Configuration → SpireMentor.

[h2]Co-op[/h2]
The coach also works in co-op runs, as host or as a client, and your teammates do not need the mod. It advises you only, but its combat search sees the whole party: your teammates' cards, block, powers and orbs, and what their cards do to you. Undo and rewind are off in co-op, since they would roll back everyone's game.

[b]AI partners (new, experimental):[/b] play co-op with AI teammates instead of, or next to, your friends. Each partner plays its own seat, character and deck with its own copy of the coach.
[list]
[*]Multiplayer → Host shows a [b]With AI partners[/b] entry: a co-op run on your PC alone.
[*]A lobby you host gets [b]Add AI partner[/b] / [b]Remove AI partner[/b] tiles (up to three). Friends join as usual and do not need the mod.
[*][b]Click an AI partner in the lobby[/b] to change its character (right-click goes back). Each partner seat remembers its last pick.
[*]Save and continue work: loading the run brings the partners back.
[*]When a partner's best move needs your setup (your Vulnerable on its target, your block on it), it waits up to 10 seconds for it; the settings ([i]Co-op AI partners[/i]) change that (0-60 s) and can make it wait for your first play, or until you end your turn, before it moves.
[*]Done setting up? The toolbar's [b]Partner go[/b] (or [b]Shift+F6[/b]) makes a waiting partner play now.
[/list]
Each partner runs one more advisor process while the run lasts, so expect more CPU use. It is new: if a partner gets stuck or acts strangely, please send a bug report (Ctrl+Shift+B).

[h2]The workbench[/h2]
The toolbar's [b]Workbench → Open workbench[/b] opens a page in your browser that follows your run as you play: every decision with what the AI advised, regret reviews and search trees, the run tree (click a save point to rewind the real game), replays and a combat sandbox. [b]Workbench → Copy state[/b] (or Ctrl+Shift+C) puts the current position on the clipboard; paste it into the workbench's [b]Import state[/b] to try other lines. It runs entirely on your machine ([i]127.0.0.1:8079[/i]).

[h2]What it does on your machine[/h2]
[list]
[*]When the coach is on, the mod starts the bundled [b]SimAdvisor.exe[/b] in the background and talks to it over a local connection ([i]127.0.0.1:9002[/i]). Nothing leaves your computer unless you send a bug report. The exe is not code-signed, so Windows SmartScreen may ask about it the first time.
[*][b]Autopilot mode[/b] (off by default) lets an AI play whole runs on its own. It turns tutorials off and makes every character selectable on your [b]modded[/b] profile. The game keeps modded progress separate from your normal save, so your unmodded profile is never touched. Advisor mode and F6/F7 never change your save.
[/list]

[h2]Files[/h2]
Config: [i]%LOCALAPPDATA%\SpireMentor\SpireMentor.conf[/i]
Logs: [i]%LOCALAPPDATA%\SpireMentor\[/i]

[h2]Documentation[/h2]
How the AI works and how well it plays: [url=https://tfriedel.github.io/spire-mentor/index.html]tfriedel.github.io/spire-mentor[/url]

